1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Kusari gives AI trading agents onchain limits and an owner-controlled ENS kill switch.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:15,000
This is a recorded product walkthrough using real Kusari screens and earlier Sepolia receipts.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:22,000
The agent proposes trades from a shared funded vault. It cannot withdraw the vault's funds.

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Public normal runs ask Gemini for a trade of up to one test kUSD, or a hold.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:38,000
The captured owner policy allows five kUSD per trade, one hundred per day, and two percent
pool-price impact.

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:45,000
The Uniswap v4 hook checks the signed request, ENS authorization and spending policy.

7
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:52,000
After execution, it checks actual output and price impact. Rejection rolls back the entire swap.

8
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:59,000
The ENS identity is alpha.kusari-pramod.eth. The owner controls the agent's authority.

9
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Its policy is ABI-encoded resolver data under kusari.policy, not an ordinary editable text limit.

10
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:13,000
In this earlier rehearsal, Gemini requested five kUSD within the owner's limit. The transaction
executed.

11
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:20,000
These are recorded receipts. Public normal runs are separately capped at one kUSD.

12
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Poisoned news persuaded the deliberately gullible demonstration agent to request ninety-five kUSD
against a five kUSD cap.

13
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:36,000
The hook reverted that transaction with ExceedsPerSwap. The failed request did not spend vault
tokens.

14
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:44,000
The owner then revoked the agent's ENS role. Revocation applies after its transaction confirms.

15
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Even a small 0.1 kUSD trade then failed with NotAuthorized. A valid agent signature was not
enough.

16
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:59,000
Only the owner can grant that role again. The earlier rehearsal restored the agent's authorization.

17
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:06,000
After restoration, a 0.1 kUSD swap succeeded. Every displayed outcome links to a Sepolia receipt.

18
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:15,000
Agent chain reads and signed transaction submissions use Anon-RPC through the Nox mixnet.

19
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:24,000
Routing observations are not proof of anonymity. Transactions stay public, and the wallet uses its
own RPC.

20
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:34,000
The shared demo is the main judging path. Personal onboarding is beta; the separate session-vault
experiment is not shown here.

21
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Try the demo, inspect the source and verify the receipts. AI proposes; the owner sets authority; the
contracts enforce it.
